<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.4.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02396</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.4.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>77d935b4-0a30-4780-8b40-e08dd1c07f34</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="8cb61b91-f898-4326-a943-82a15a7e45cf" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para><emphasis>Select three </emphasis>expressions that are perfect squares.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(9x^2+24x+16\), \((7-3x)^2\), \((1-2x)(-2x+1)\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answers are: \(9x^2+24x+16\), \((7-3x)^2\), \((1-2x)(-2x+1)\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="90cd1566-01f1-4ae5-869d-6ae4f7672f8e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Find the missing number that makes the expression a perfect square.</para>
      <para>\(49x^2-\_\_\_\_\_\_x+16\)<para>Enter the missing number</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(49x^2−56x+16\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 56. \(49x^2−56x+16\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="5ea07411-6348-4906-95df-e7ae55167a0c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(36x^2+\_\_\_\_\_\_x+4\)
          <para> Enter the missing number. </para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(36x^2+24x+4\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 24. \(36x^2+24x+4\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="43a1355d-8fcf-463e-80df-1c6958cb6228" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4x^2-\_\_\_\_\_\_x+25\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(4x^2−20x+25\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 20. \(4x^2−20x+25\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="41350ad7-d9ba-47e7-a761-ade2a2fdeedf" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(9x^2+\_\_\_\_\_\_x+9\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(9x^2+18x+9\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 18. \(9x^2+18x+9\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="dbbde4b2-9b7d-44f3-b2e8-f427a5464c70" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(121x^2+\_\_\_\_\_\_x+9\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(121x^2+66x+9\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 66. \(121x^2+66x+9\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="bb7a6593-60a3-4aa1-946a-bb11e82f2fe7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> Choose the completely factored form of the expression.</para>
      <para>\(49x^2-56x+16\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((7x+4)^2\)</para><para>\((49x-16)^2\)</para><para>\((7x-4)^2\)</para><para>\((28x-11)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((7x-4)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((7x-4)^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="f5a6787e-5e5a-4596-a765-05d0ddd12951" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(36x^2+24x+4\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((6x-2)^2\)</para><para>\((36x+4)^2\)</para><para>\((6x+2)^2\)</para><para>\(4(3x+1)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(4(3x+1)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is: \(4(3x+1)^2\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="2a0b4c94-e582-4c27-9243-e427297fef83" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4x^2-20x+25\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>(\(10x+7)^2\)</para><para>\((2x-5)^2\)</para><para>\((4x-25)^2\)</para><para>\((2x+5)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((2x-5)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((2x-5)^2\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="47a081a1-7b99-457b-ae6b-1aac8dbf22ba" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(121x^2+66x+9\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((11x+3)^2\)</para><para>\((121x-9)^2\)</para><para>\((3x-3)^2\)</para><para>\((11x-3)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((11x+3)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.1 and 9.4.2.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((11x+3)^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="a5d43333-fc76-4205-ba6c-38de749d4f55" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Find the missing number that makes the expression a perfect square.</para>
      <para>\(9x^2+42x+\_\_\_\_\_\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(9x^2+42x+49\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 49. \(9x^2+42x+49)\.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="2bb17e4e-fb1e-45a6-87ac-e8182620fa2e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \(49x^2-28x+\_\_\_\_\_\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(49x^2-28x+4\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.
      </para><para>The correct answer is 4. \(49x^2-28x+4\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="bb643eb6-5cbe-42bd-8c88-4195f7ffe5b5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(25x^2+110x+\_\_\_\_\_\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(25x^2+110x+121\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 121. \(25x^2+110x+121\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="94ad2467-b43a-44ae-a6f1-9004b90c96fe" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(64x^2-144x+\_\_\_\_\_\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(64x^2-144x+81\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 81. \(64x^2-144x+81\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="c0fcba19-49c5-4e46-8f68-bca31c8a2a84" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4x^2+24x+\_\_\_\_\_\)
          <para> Enter the missing number.</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(4x^2+24x+36\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 36. \(4x^2+24x+36\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="4130d641-f12b-4805-8167-6c38b3e23a93" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Based on your responses in question 4 above, choose the factored form of the expression.</para>
      <para>\(9x^2+42x+\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((3x+7)^2\)</para><para>\((9x-21)^2\)</para><para>\((3x-7)^2\)</para><para>\((9x+3)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((3x+7)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((3x+7)^2\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="61886b43-e74d-4a1f-94ec-397886fad3c0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(49x^2-28x+\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((4x+7)^2\)</para><para>\((7x+2)^2\)</para><para>\((7x-2)^2\)</para><para>\((7x+7)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((7x-2)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((7x-2)^2\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="912afd57-5fcc-4819-8456-ba63574d40f3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(25x^2+110x+\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((5x-11)^2\)</para><para>\((11x+5)^2\)</para><para>\((11x-5)^2\)</para><para>\((5x+11)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((5x+11)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((5x+11)^2\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="36112b04-a847-4368-9589-fd637f961558" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(64x^2-144x+\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((72x-17)^2\)</para><para>\((8x-9)^2\)</para><para>\((64x-9)^2\)</para><para>\((8x+9)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((8x-9)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((8x-9)^2\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="0104e28c-b9ff-4c13-a368-c57767dcad9f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4x^2+24x+\_\_\_\_\_\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2x-6)^2\)</para><para>\((4x-26)^2\)</para><para>\((2x+6)^2\)</para><para>\((x+6)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((2x+6)^2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para> The correct answer is: \((2x+6)^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="646f9b6b-4d47-4645-8ba1-973246df0c71" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each expression, find the value of \(c\) to make a perfect square in standard form \((ax^2+bx+c)\).</para>
      <para>\(4x^2+4x+c\)
          <para> Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(4x^2+4x+1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 1. \(4x^2+4x+1\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="9cbbc656-1839-4d22-9351-0148dd6af177" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(25x^2-30x+c\)
          <para> Enter the value of \(c\).</para>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(25x^2−30x+9\) </para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 9. \(25x^2−30x+9\) . </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="5f115dc3-9078-43ec-96cb-a75ade162d8e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Use the value of \(c\) needed to make the expression a perfect square (from the previous question). Then, solve each equation.</para>
      <para>\(4x^2+4x+c=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=\frac12\)</para><para>\(x=-\frac12\)</para><para>\(x=\frac32\)</para><para>\(x=-\frac32\)</para><para>\(x=2\)</para><para>\(x=\frac16\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-\frac12\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.3 – 9.4.5.</para><para>The correct answer is: \(-\frac12\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="02ccc131-0826-45b1-9c8f-15eb1f7ae2c9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(25x^2-30x+c=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=\frac12\)</para><para>\(x=-\frac45\)</para><para>\(x=\frac25\)</para><para>\(x = 4\)</para><para>\(x = 5\)</para><para>\(x=\frac35\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(x=\frac35\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.4.3 – 9.4.5.</para><para>The correct answer is: \(x=\frac35\).
      </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
